# App version bump checklist

When incrementing the MeepleUp app version (e.g. for a new store release), update **all** of the following. Never bump only some of them.

## 1. Version string (e.g. `1.0.5` → `1.0.6`)

- **app.json** — `expo.version`
- **package.json** — `version`
- **ios/MeepleUp/Info.plist** — `CFBundleShortVersionString`
- **ios/MeepleUp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj** — `MARKETING_VERSION` (Debug and Release)
- **android/app/build.gradle** — `versionName`

## 2. iOS build number (integer, always increase)

- **app.json** — `expo.ios.buildNumber` (string)
- **ios/MeepleUp/Info.plist** — `CFBundleVersion`
- **ios/MeepleUp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj** — `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` (Debug and Release)

**EAS production builds:** `eas.json` enables `"autoIncrement": true` on the `production` profile with `cli.appVersionSource: local`. For each **EAS Build** with that profile, the CLI bumps iOS build number / Android `versionCode` and updates native files + `app.json` so you do not have to bump them by hand before every build. **Commit** the version files after a successful build so the repo stays the source of truth. For marketing version bumps (section 1), still update all listed files manually.

**Optional (Expo-recommended):** set `cli.appVersionSource` to `remote` and use `eas build:version:set` / `eas build:version:sync` so build numbers live on EAS servers and you do not rely on committing after each build ([App version management](https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/app-versions/)).

## 3. Android version code (integer, always increase)

- **app.json** — `expo.android.versionCode`
- **android/app/build.gradle** — `versionCode`

## Summary

| Location | Version field | Build/code field |
|----------|----------------|------------------|
| app.json | `version` | `ios.buildNumber`, `android.versionCode` |
| package.json | `version` | — |
| ios/MeepleUp/Info.plist | `CFBundleShortVersionString` | `CFBundleVersion` |
| ios/.../project.pbxproj | `MARKETING_VERSION` | `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` |
| android/app/build.gradle | `versionName` | `versionCode` |

Always increment both the version string and the build/version code when preparing a new store submission.
